                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "gugelhupfs"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0fa2e954-bb5e-37b6-9841-193fc4330633",
                        "entry_id": "4bfe780e-82a0-3095-b7b0-2951687d4ec1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Alternative letter-case form of Gugelhupf."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "alt-of",
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "70223ea8-07bf-4269-ae47-78f9c3d452b7",
                                "sense_id": "0fa2e954-bb5e-37b6-9841-193fc4330633",
                                "text": "With the back of a spoon make a small hollow around centre of gugelhupf – to keep the cake base more level when cooked."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b9b69366-5b3b-4b47-b6a7-e682e02e9a41",
                                "sense_id": "0fa2e954-bb5e-37b6-9841-193fc4330633",
                                "text": "When the gugelhupf is cold, dust lightly with icing sugar, then make the icing. Sieve the icing sugar into a bowl and blend with enough rum to make a thin icing. Drizzle half of the icing over the gugelhupf."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "49f64b5a-3ea5-4af5-8057-956a0416e8e3",
                                "sense_id": "0fa2e954-bb5e-37b6-9841-193fc4330633",
                                "text": "When the gugelhupf is almost completely risen, set a rack at the lower third of the oven and preheat to 375 degrees."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dd5485e8-d909-4708-80c6-6af1f2bcef72",
                                "sense_id": "0fa2e954-bb5e-37b6-9841-193fc4330633",
                                "text": "However, if you arrived a quarter of an hour before that, and ordered your coffee and whipped cream, you didn’t have to pay the five-kreuzer supplement for the music, only the standard thirty for coffee and fifteen for a slice of gugelhupf cake."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "baf5a440-4b83-467c-b88e-b95296dbfa1b",
                                "sense_id": "0fa2e954-bb5e-37b6-9841-193fc4330633",
                                "text": "It would be a pity not to try something to eat – for a ‘lighter’ alternative many cafés serve slices of gugelhupf, a Viennese marbled madeira cake, a simply delicious companion to coffee."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "57d84f9f-1883-45bb-84ad-2ac849dc2a46",
                                "sense_id": "0fa2e954-bb5e-37b6-9841-193fc4330633",
                                "text": "I baked gugelhupfs in great varieties with raisins or with coconut or with chocolate. There was always a gugelhupf in the house and as these cakes are so large there was plenty of it and who ever came to visit us was treated to a slice of it."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "42ca926b-89ba-4e0a-93d7-9dab65e8948b",
                                "sense_id": "0fa2e954-bb5e-37b6-9841-193fc4330633",
                                "text": "Place cold gugelhupf in oven and bake until top is light golden brown and cake tester comes out clean, about 40 to 45 minutes (a smaller pan may take a few minutes longer), rotating pan front to back halfway through."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
